# Portfolio Dashboard Project Structure

This is an enterprise fullstack application with the following architecture:

## Project Overview
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and React 19
- **Backend**: FastAPI with Python 3.x, SQLAlchemy, and PostgreSQL
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with Alembic migrations
- **Deployment**: Docker Compose for development, AWS for production
- **Authentication**: Enterprise-grade authentication system

## Directory Structure
```
portfolio-dashboard/
├── frontend/                 # Next.js frontend application
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── app/             # Next.js App Router pages and layouts
│   │   ├── hooks/           # Custom React hooks
│   │   └── lib/             # Utility functions and configurations
│   ├── package.json         # Frontend dependencies
│   └── tailwind.config.js   # Tailwind CSS configuration
├── backend/                  # FastAPI backend application
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── api/             # API route handlers
│   │   ├── core/            # Core application logic
│   │   ├── crud/            # Database CRUD operations
│   │   ├── models/          # SQLAlchemy models
│   │   ├── schemas/         # Pydantic schemas
│   │   ├── services/        # Business logic services
│   │   └── utils/           # Utility functions
│   ├── alembic/             # Database migrations
│   ├── tests/               # Backend tests
│   └── requirements.txt     # Python dependencies
├── database/                 # Database-related files
├── docs/                    # Project documentation
├── docker-compose.yml       # Development environment setup
├── Makefile                 # Development commands
└── README.md               # Project overview
```

## Key Files
- [Makefile](mdc:Makefile) - Development commands (`make setup`, `make dev`, `make test`)
- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Development environment
- [frontend/package.json](mdc:frontend/package.json) - Frontend dependencies and scripts
- [backend/requirements.txt](mdc:backend/requirements.txt) - Backend dependencies
- [frontend/tsconfig.json](mdc:frontend/tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
- [frontend/tailwind.config.js](mdc:frontend/tailwind.config.js) - Tailwind CSS configuration

## Development Workflow
1. Use `make setup` to install dependencies
2. Use `make dev` to start development environment
3. Use `make test` to run tests
4. Use `make lint` to run linters
5. Use `make build` to build for production

